The '''Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone''' ({{lang|ca|Zona Franca de Sant Cristòfor}}) is a {{w|free trade zone}} in [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]], established in 1978. It is the largest free trade zone in Lurandia and a major re-export centre for goods moving between Illypnia, Fosia, and Kaftia. The zone encompasses the entire [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|comarca of Sant Cristòfor]] together with the comarcas of [[Marjal del Canal]] and [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]], covering a total area of 4,909 km² with a combined population of approximately 9.1 million (2026). The zone employs approximately 85,000 workers in manufacturing, warehousing, and logistics.

