[[Portnou]], the capital of [[Marjal del Canal]], serves as the canal's western terminus and the zone's principal port, handling container transshipment, bulk cargo, and petroleum products. The city of [[Sant Cristòfor]], capital of the eponymous comarca, is the zone's commercial and financial centre, hosting the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and the regional headquarters of major international banks. [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]] hosts the majority of the zone's manufacturing and assembly operations, concentrated around the canal corridor and [[Lake Alvarado]].

== History ==

The Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone was established in 1978, five years after reunification, as part of the government's strategy to integrate the canal corridor into the national economy and attract foreign investment. The zone was designated across the three comarcas that formed the core of the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area and the canal's western approach, taking advantage of the existing port infrastructure at Portnou and the city's position at the junction of Illypnian, Fosian, and Kaftian trade routes.

The designation of the zone built upon the institutional framework of the [[Twelve Guarantees]], which provided legal certainty for commercial operations and protected the rights of businesses operating within the zone. Companies operating in the zone benefit from reduced corporate tax rates, customs exemptions for imported inputs, and streamlined regulatory procedures.

During the 1980s and 1990s, the zone developed as a major centre for light manufacturing, warehousing, and re-export. The establishment of the [[BTPMEU]] in 1998 further enhanced the zone's role, as goods manufactured within the zone could be exported to BTPMEU member states under preferential tariff terms.

== Economic activity ==

The zone hosts approximately 85,000 workers across three principal sectors:

* Manufacturing — including garment assembly, electronics assembly, automotive {{w|completely knocked down|CKD}} assembly, and consumer goods packaging, concentrated in [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]]
* Warehousing and distribution — serving as a re-export hub for goods moving between the three continental markets, concentrated in [[Marjal del Canal]] and the port of [[Portnou]]
* Logistics and trade services — including freight forwarding, customs brokerage, and supply chain management, concentrated in the city of [[Sant Cristòfor]]

== Tax and regulatory framework ==

Companies operating within the Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone benefit from:

* Reduced corporate tax rate (below the national standard of 25 per cent)
* {{w|Customs|Customs exemptions}} on imported raw materials, components, and capital goods used within the zone
* Streamlined licensing and permitting procedures
* {{w|Duty-free shop|Duty-free}} re-export of manufactured goods

The zone is administered by the [[Government of Balboa]], with customs enforcement handled by the national customs service under the framework of the [[Adonian Community]].

